    "examples": [
      {
        "question_text": "Factorise by taking out a negative common factor.\na. $-14x-21$\nb. $-11+7t$",
        "solution_text": "a. The numerical HCF is $7$. Divide both terms by $-7$.\n$-14x-21=-7(2x+3)$\nCheck: $-7(2x+3)=-14x-21$.\nb. The HCF is $1$, so take out $-1$.\n$-11+7t=-(11-7t)$\nCheck: $-(11-7t)=-11+7t$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Factorise by taking out a negative common factor.\na. $-18a^2+24a$\nb. $-15uv-10vw-25uvw$\nc. $-8+14r^2$",
        "solution_text": "a. The HCF is $6a$. Divide each term by $-6a$.\n$-18a^2+24a=-6a(3a-4)$\nCheck: $-6a(3a-4)=-18a^2+24a$.\nb. The HCF is $5v$. Divide all three terms by $-5v$.\n$-15uv-10vw-25uvw=-5v(3u+2w+5uw)$\nCheck: $-5v(3u+2w+5uw)=-15uv-10vw-25uvw$.\nc. The HCF is $2$. There is no variable common to both terms.\n$-8+14r^2=-2(4-7r^2)$\nCheck: $-2(4-7r^2)=-8+14r^2$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Factorise $-14p-21q+28$ by taking out a negative common factor.",
        "solution_text": "The numerical HCF is $7$. Divide every term by $-7$: $-14p\\div(-7)=2p$, $-21q\\div(-7)=3q$ and $28\\div(-7)=-4$.\n$\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}-14p-21q+28\\\\&=-7(2p+3q-4)\\end{aligned}$\nCheck: $-7(2p+3q-4)=-14p-21q+28$."
      }
    ],
